+        <t indent="0" pn="section-4.2-1">When an IPv6 node places a call to another IPv6 node, it <bcp14>SHOULD</bcp14> follow the procedures in <xref target="6" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="6"/> and <xref target="7" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="7"/> for signalling UNI 3.0/3.1 SVCs <xref target="9" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="9"/> and negotiating MTU.  The default IP MTU size on a LL is 9180 bytes as specified in <xref target="7" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="7"/>.</t>
